{"name":"Enchanted Wood","hex":"#94895f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"enchanted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of enchant"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Charmed, delighted, enraptured.","Under the influence of enchantment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enchanted"},{"term":"wood","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The substance making up the central part of the trunk and branches of a tree. Used as a material for construction, to manufacture various items, etc. or as fuel.","The wood from a particular species of tree."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover or plant with trees.","To hide behind trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dream Cycle","blocks":[{"text":"The Dream Cycle is a series of short stories and novellas by author H. P. Lovecraft (1890–1937). Written between 1918 and 1932, they are about the \"Dreamlands\", a vast alternate dimension that can only be entered via dreams. The Dreamlands are described as lying deeper than space, matter and time, and are a \"limitless vacua beyond all thought and entity\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/32/Dreamworld-map.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream_Cycle"},{"title":"The Faraway Tree","blocks":[{"text":"The Faraway Tree is a series of popular novels for children by British author Enid Blyton. The titles in the series are The Enchanted Wood (1939), The Magic Faraway Tree (1943), The Folk of the Faraway Tree (1946) and Up the Faraway Tree (1951)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/51/The_Magic_Faraway_Tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Faraway_Tree"},{"title":"Enchanted (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Enchanted is a 2007 American live action/animated musical fantasy comedy film directed by Kevin Lima and written by Bill Kelly. Co-produced by Walt Disney Pictures, Josephson Entertainment, and Right Coast Productions, the film stars Amy Adams, Patrick Dempsey, James Marsden, Timothy Spall, Idina Menzel, and Susan Sarandon, with Julie Andrews as the narrator. It focuses on an archetypal Disney princess-to-be named Giselle, who is exiled from her animated world into the live-action world of the New York metropolitan area, where she falls in love with a divorce lawyer."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2a/Enchantedposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enchanted_(film)"},{"title":"Wood","blocks":[{"text":"Wood is a natural, lignocellulosic material derived primarily from the secondary xylem of trees and other woody plants, where it provides mechanical support and in the functional sapwood, conducts water and dissolved minerals. Being a natural material, it is characterized as an organic material – a natural composite of cellulosic fibers that are strong in tension and embedded in a matrix of lignin and hemicelluloses that resists compression."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/16_wood_samples.jpg/330px-16_wood_samples.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b6/The_Enchanted_Wood_cover.jpg/250px-The_Enchanted_Wood_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b6/The_Enchanted_Wood_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b6/The_Enchanted_Wood_cover.jpg/250px-The_Enchanted_Wood_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=p